% protocol_domain — the director interface, the generic INTERFACE PACKAGE (specialist-tree s-404d001f, brief v2 §9, §11:
% specialist → protocol ← director, a DAG; metis-lang spec/15 amendment 2): the REPORTS a
% specialist's tick gives the director (status, active, done, stuck, want, release) and the GRANTS the director gives a
% specialist (grant, goal), over two abstract types the composition makes concrete — domain (the specialists'
% names, S) and resource (R). Neither side names the other: both include this file,
% `include "iface/protocol_domain.llp".` (found under METIS_HOME: one module for every world and catalog; no copies).
catalog protocol_domain 1.
provenance text "the tick's protocol: reports in, grants out, over abstract specialists and resources" "2026-10-25".
layers (dyn).
types (domain resource).
type tick__status {running success failure idle}.

namespace proto produce (dyn).

% ── the reports (a specialist's tick, read by the director) ──
pred tick__status(domain, tick__status) : proto.   % the agent's reading of D's last tick (spec/15 §4.4: from its rows)
pred tick__active(domain) : proto.                 % D's own trigger fired (step 3: the inversion)
pred tick__done(domain) : proto.                   % D's goal is met
pred tick__stuck(domain) : proto.                  % D cannot go on

pred tick__want(domain, resource) : proto.         % D asks for R (kept asked until granted, once per need)
pred tick__release(domain, resource) : proto.      % D is done with R (its goal may go on: a cook releases the pot, then serves)

% ── the grants (the director's, read by a specialist) ──
pred tick__grant(domain, resource) : proto.        % D holds R: only the holder's commands reach the world
pred tick__goal(domain) : proto.                   % D has a goal from the director (the path's running branch)
pred tick__revoke(domain, resource) : proto.       % the director's: D no longer holds R (the agent retracts the grant)
